{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789779179,"nonce":"sGT86+3kFWa82t4RuRXsyRveV6U=","title":"Every tuple literal allocates: alloca promotion and no scalarization of insertvalue webs","message":"alloca_promote treats InsertValue and ExtractValue on an alloca as escapes,\nso the alloca the SSA builds a tuple literal in becomes a malloc on every\nconstruction; nothing frees it, and no pass scalarizes an aggregate SSA\nvalue that is only built by insertvalue, read by extractvalue and carried\nby phis. A loop `p = step(p, v, dt)` with step inlined allocates 16 bytes\nper iteration and spends its time in the allocator and the collector\n(2 s for 2M iterations; PyPy 27 ms).\n\nFix, in order:\n1. A HIR pass that scalarizes insertvalue/extractvalue/phi webs into\n   per-field values, rematerializing an aggregate only at an escaping use\n   (call argument, return, store, insertion into another aggregate).\n2. alloca_promote keeps an aggregate-typed alloca on the stack when every\n   use is a value use; the LLVM backend then hoists fixed-size allocas to\n   the entry block so a loop does not grow the stack per iteration.","files":null}]}